[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes,calc}
\coordinate (B) at (0,0);
\coordinate (A) at (0,3);
\coordinate (C) at (4,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,left] {$c$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,below] {$a$};
\draw (C)--(A) node[midway,above right] {$b$};
\coordinate (ra1) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (ra2) at ($(B)!0.3cm!(C)$);
\draw (ra1)--($(ra1)+(ra2)-(B)$)--(ra2);
\pic[draw,"$x$",angle radius=0.7cm,angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=B--A--C};
\pic[draw,"$90^{\circ}-x$",angle radius=0.7cm,angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=A--C--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Write $\sin x$ and $\sin(90^{\circ}-x)$ as ratios of $a$, $b$ and $c$, and hence complete $\sin(90^{\circ}-x)=\cos\ldots$
